# What belongs in this repo: everything needed to build, test, document, and
# release the package from a fresh clone — sources, tests, docs, examples,
# `scripts/`, `uv.lock`, and `agentkit/py.typed`. Nothing below should ever
# match one of those; `make check` and a clean `git status` after a full run
# are the two things that prove it.

# ── Python bytecode / native artifacts ──────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python

# ── Distribution / packaging ────────────────────────────────────────────────
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
*.egg
wheels/
# `agentkit/py.typed` is a PACKAGED marker file (PEP 561) that tells type
# checkers the wheel ships inline types. Nothing above matches it — this note
# exists so a future broad pattern like `*.typed` is recognised as a mistake.

# ── Virtualenvs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
env/
.tox/
.nox/
# A locally pinned interpreter is a personal choice; CI installs its own via
# `uv python install`, and the supported range lives in `pyproject.toml`.
.python-version

# ── Test / type / lint caches ───────────────────────────────────────────────
.hypothesis/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ── Coverage ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `[tool.coverage.run] parallel = true` makes coverage write per-process data
# files named `.coverage.<host>.<pid>.<random>` alongside the combined
# `.coverage`. A bare `.coverage` pattern does NOT match those, so every
# `make cov` run would otherwise leave a fistful of untracked binaries.
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
coverage.json
htmlcov/

# ── Mutation testing ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `scripts/mutants.py` snapshots the files it rewrites here so a hard-killed
# run is recoverable (the next invocation restores from it automatically). It
# only exists mid-run, or after a crash — never something to commit.
.mutants-backup/

# ── Credentials and local environment ───────────────────────────────────────
# This framework resolves provider keys from the environment
# (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, OPENAI_API_KEY, DEEPSEEK_API_KEY, OPENROUTER_API_KEY),
# so contributors WILL create local env files while working on the registry
# and the provider adapters. A key committed to a public repo is the single
# worst thing this file can fail to prevent — the patterns below are
# deliberately broad, with an explicit escape hatch for a committed template.
.env
.env.*
*.env
.envrc
!.env.example
!.env.template
secrets/
secrets.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
credentials.json
service-account*.json

# ── mkdocs build output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
site/

# ── Editors ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.sublime-workspace
*.sublime-project
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Claude Code: project-shared settings (`.claude/settings.json`) are worth
# committing; per-developer overrides are not.
.claude/settings.local.json

# ── OS cruft ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# ── Merge / patch leftovers ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Committing one of these silently ships conflict markers as real code.
*.orig
*.rej
*.bak
